1. Introduction
The Automated Turret Radar System is a project designed to detect nearby objects, automatically aim toward them, and trigger a simulated firing sequence. The system integrates sensors, actuators, and visual/auditory indicators to create a functional demonstration of real‑world mechatronic principles such as scanning, targeting, and feedback control.
This project showcases the interaction between hardware components (servos, ultrasonic sensor, LEDs, buzzer) and software logic running on an Arduino microcontroller.
